==============================================================================
VCACHE-3D  --  thermal model (steady state, one dielet column)
==============================================================================

layer                   material      thk um   k W/mK     R K/W
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
base die silicon        Si              85.0    110.0     0.073
hybrid bond interface   SiO2/Cu          0.2     25.0     0.001
cache dielet silicon    Si              36.0    110.0     0.031
dielet backside TIM     TIM             25.0      5.0     0.473
copper lid              Cu             800.0    390.0     0.194
lid to ambient          convection                        4.200
                                                     ----------
total, junction to air                                    4.972

Steady-state temperatures vs base-die power under the dielet
  (dielet self-heating fixed at 0.62 W, ambient 45 C)

 P_base (W)  T_base (C)  T_dielet (C)  T_lid (C)   state
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
          2        54.5          54.4       53.4   ok
          4        61.0          60.8       59.1   ok
          6        67.4          67.1       64.9   ok
          8        73.9          73.5       70.6   ok
         10        80.3          79.9       76.3   ok
         12        86.8          86.2       82.0   ok
         14        93.3          92.6       87.7   ok
         16        99.7          99.0       93.4   throttling
         18       106.2         105.3       99.1   OVER LIMIT
         20       112.7         111.7      104.8   OVER LIMIT
         24       125.6         124.4      116.3   OVER LIMIT
         28       138.5         137.2      127.7   OVER LIMIT

Design point: 12 W core power under the dielet
  base-die junction     86.8 C
  dielet junction       86.2 C   (margin to 105 C limit: 18.8 C)
  lid                   82.0 C
  same column without a dielet     83.5 C
  thermal penalty of stacking       3.3 C (bond interface + 36 um of silicon + dielet self-heat)

  throttle asserts above ~16 W of local core power;
  the 105 C limit is reached at ~18 W, so the
  throttle loop has to act before that -- which is what
  rtl/power/vc3d_thermal_throttle.v does, in 4 steps, from the 16
  on-dielet sensors filtered by the same IIR the Python golden
  model in model/vc3d_model.py checks (s += (target - s) >> 6).

Transient behaviour
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dielet heat capacity      0.6 mJ/K
  time constant to the lid  3.0 ms
  a 0.6 W step therefore moves the dielet 2.9 C with a 3 ms tail,
  which is why the throttle samples at 1 kHz and filters with a
  6-bit-shift IIR rather than reacting to single-sample noise.

Conclusions carried into the design
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * the dielet is thinned to 36 um -- at 100 um it adds 3x the
    vertical resistance and the base die loses ~4 C of headroom;
  * the dielet runs at 0.75 V and 1.5 GHz, not at core voltage;
    dropping it to core voltage would roughly triple its dynamic
    power and eat the margin computed above;
  * per-bank sleep matters: 90 % retention saves 0.49 W per dielet,
    which is most of the idle thermal budget;
  * the bond field is also the best heat path between the dies, so
    the floorplan spreads the 1376 pads across the die edge rather
    than clustering them (pd/scripts/floorplan_cache.tcl).
